23-year  history  the pre-trial chamber said that there  might be a protracted process  um and the types of cases that we've  seen coming before the court  have gone on for years and years and  years and then  once we saw the word protracted that  kind of signified to us that although  we're now very much in the investigation  stage that there still could be  further delays and we'd be very very  concerned with that icc involvement in  the struggle between israelis and  palestinians  could shine a light on other state  injustices but what's less certain  is whether it will help or hinder the  troubled search for peace  in the middle east neve barker al  jazeera
 

